==Parameters==
All omitted "optional" fields will be hidden if empty.

===name===
The name of the special attack '''exactly''' as it appears in game (identical case and spacing).

===weapon===
Name of every weapon that uses the special attack of the same name.

===image===
The inventory image of the ''primary'' weapon using this spec, formatted as <nowiki>[[File:Image.png]]</nowiki>. Ideally in [[Wikipedia:Portable Network Graphics|PNG]] format. For specs with multiple versions or sources (such as poisoned dragon daggers' ''puncture'', or Dragon and crystal halberds' ''sweep'', all images should be included.

===style===
The general type of the special attack, use weapon's generic style if not specified. Accepted values are: Melee, Ranged, Magic, Melee (crush), Melee (slash), Melee (stab).
* [[Dragon dagger]]: Melee (slash)
* [[Voidwaker]]: Magic
* [[Barrelchest anchor]]: Melee

===target===
Describes how the special attack targets enemies while in multi-combat areas. Accepted values: single, burst, chain, cleave, self, varies. See [[Multicombat area#Area-of-effect_attacks]] for clarifications.

===maxtargets===
(optional)
Specify the maximum number of targets that can be hit in multicombat areas.

===range===
(optional)
Multiple cases based on the target. Only use this if the range of a single target spec deviates from the weapon's range, or to specify the number of tiles.
* [[Dragon halberd]]: 1×3
* [[Corrupted volatile nightmare staff]]: 6
* [[Dragon crossbow]]: 3×3
* [[Dinh's Bulwark]]: 11×11
* [[Rune thrownaxe]]: 7×7

===energy===
Cost in special energy. Format as "50%".
For [[Soulreaper axe]], Seasonal, and potential future charge-based weapons, format as "X-Y charges" 
ie: 1-20 charges

===anim===
The gif of the special attack in action., formatted as <nowiki>[[File:Spec.gif]]</nowiki>

===seasonal===
(Optional)
Whether this spec is only available during certain temporary game modes/worlds, such as leagues, deadman, gridmaster, etc. Format as <nowiki>[[name]]</nowiki> of the game mode(s).

===requirements===
(optional)
Used when there are non-skill requirements to use a special attack. Format as <nowiki>[[Quest name]]</nowiki>.

===attack_roll===
(optional)
Modifiers to the accuracy roll, Format as: +15%, or "True strike" when the roll is skipped.
For multi-hit specs, always use "/" to separate hits, even if they use the same modifier.
* [[Dragon halberd]]: +0%/-20%
* [[Dragon dagger]]: +15%/+15%

===defence_roll===
(optional)
Specifies when the accuracy is hard-coded to roll against a specific defensive stat. Accepted values are: Melee, Ranged, Magic, Melee (crush), Melee (slash), Melee (stab), Varies.

===damage_roll===
(optional)
Modifiers to the damage roll. Format as "+15%" for most cases, "+25% min hit", "15" for flat damage, and "Scales".
For multi-hit specs, always use "/" to separate hits, even if they use the same modifier.
* [[Dragon halberd]]: +10%/+10%
* [[Dragon dagger]]: +15%/+15%

===damage_type===
(optional)
If the damage type is different from the one listed in "style", or is hybrid, list it here. 
Damage over time effects are listed with ''dot''. Accepted values: Melee, Magic, Ranged, Poison, Venom, Burn, Untyped. Separate by comma when multiple are true. Only separate with "/" if multi-hits are not all the same type of damage.
* [[Voidwaker]]: Magic
* [[Saradomin sword]]: Melee, Magic

===dot===
(optional)
Damage over time. Format as Type: chance%; total; # dmg per interval
* [[Arkan blade]] Burn: 100%; 40 dmg; 1 per 4 ticks


===attack_delay===
(optional)
Number expressed in ticks required before next attack is possible. Only fill if different than base weapon or if the spec interacts with attack_delay in any other way.  Accepted values are whole numbers of ticks, and Varies.
* [[Dragon thrown axe]]: 1
* [[Eye of ayak]]: 5
* [[Granite maul]]: Varies
* [[Rune claws]]: 5

===hp===
(Optional)
How much hitpoint is restored/consumed. Formatted as "x%", or as a flat number, ''and'' "can exceed".

===pray===
(Optional)
How much prayer point is restored/consumed. Formatted as "x%", or as a flat number, ''and'' "can exceed".

===duration===
(optional)
For non-stat buffs and debuffs with a duration. Formatted in number of ticks.

===pvp===
(optional)
Set as TRUE if the spec (or weapon) is only usable in PVP. Set as FALSE if the spec (or whole weapon) is disabled in PVP

===tooltip===
The tooltip text '''exactly''' as it appears in-game (identical case, spaces, typo, innacuracies, etc). The text is obtained through hovering on the special attack bar.


